  "documents": [
    {
      "category": "Storage",
      "id": 0,
      "text": "The RAM and SSD caches are disposable acceleration. Acknowledged writes remain in object storage; losing the local cache makes queries cold again without losing committed data.",
      "title": "Cache loss does not lose data",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/DESIGN.md#persisted-pack-sketches-and-selective-reads"
    },
    {
      "category": "Storage",
      "id": 1,
      "text": "The server warms its local SSD block cache in the background. Queries can read selected vector blocks from RAM or SSD instead of downloading them from object storage.",
      "title": "Warm searches avoid remote reads",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/DESIGN.md#persisted-pack-sketches-and-selective-reads"
    },
    {
      "category": "Storage",
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Glider acknowledges a write after publishing a complete immutable log object. Roots and logs define the committed state; local caches are derived and never replace durable storage.",
      "title": "The bucket is authoritative",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/DESIGN.md#acknowledgement-and-recovery"
    },
    {
      "category": "Storage",
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A restarted server takes over the collection, fences its previous writer and replays the durable log. It serves every acknowledged write after recovery.",
      "title": "Recover after a restart",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/docs/API.md#consistency"
    },
    {
      "category": "Storage",
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Full vectors live in immutable object-store packs. In memory, the segmented engine retains the latest-ID directory, routing sketches and the unsealed log tail.",
      "title": "Immutable vector packs",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/DESIGN.md#engines-and-namespace-compatibility"
    },
    {
      "category": "Storage",
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Block bytes from RAM, SSD and object storage are authenticated against the committed block digest before decoding and scoring. Corrupt cached entries cannot become authoritative data.",
      "title": "Authenticate cached blocks",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/DESIGN.md#persisted-pack-sketches-and-selective-reads"
    },
    {
      "category": "Search",
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Search supports equality, set membership, existence, numeric comparisons and logical combinations over string metadata. The full predicate is checked against the records read for the query.",
      "title": "Filter by metadata",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/docs/API.md#filters"
    },
    {
      "category": "Search",
      "id": 7,
      "text": "Add exact: true to search all live points and evaluate the full metadata filter exhaustively. The query returns up to k matches; bounded approximate search can miss eligible points.",
      "title": "Get complete filtered results",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/docs/API.md#filters"
    },
    {
      "category": "Search",
      "id": 8,
      "text": "A filter can combine a color equality with a price range and tag membership. Conditions on the same key and different members of one filter object are ANDed.",
      "title": "Combine numeric and category filters",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/docs/API.md#filters"
    },
    {
      "category": "Search",
      "id": 9,
      "text": "Required equality predicates on declared routed metadata keys restrict candidate routing. Glider still applies the complete filter to authenticated records during reranking.",
      "title": "Route declared filter keys",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/DESIGN.md#persisted-pack-sketches-and-selective-reads"
    },
    {
      "category": "Search",
      "id": 10,
      "text": "A collection has a fixed dimension and a fixed metric: squared Euclidean, Manhattan or cosine. Cosine vectors and queries must have nonzero norm and are normalized by the engine.",
      "title": "Choose your distance metric",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/DESIGN.md#engines-and-namespace-compatibility"
    },
    {
      "category": "Search",
      "id": 11,
      "text": "Exact search scores every live matching vector and sorts by distance then ID. Approximate query results are evaluated against exact neighbors using recall at k.",
      "title": "Exact search is the recall oracle",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/docs/API.md#post-v1query"
    },
    {
      "category": "Concurrency",
      "id": 12,
      "text": "Reader threads search immutable published views while the committer accepts writes. Each query observes a consistent snapshot; readers do not wait behind a long object-store write.",
      "title": "Queries and writes run together",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/DESIGN.md#concurrent-queries-on-published-views-m34"
    },
    {
      "category": "Concurrency",
      "id": 13,
      "text": "A query sent after a successful write acknowledgement observes that write. A snapshot never exposes a partially applied write group or a partially published root.",
      "title": "Read your acknowledged writes",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/docs/API.md#consistency"
    },
    {
      "category": "Concurrency",
      "id": 14,
      "text": "Recent acknowledged writes stay in the in-memory log tail until sealing. Selective queries scan that tail exactly and merge it with neighbors reranked from selected immutable blocks.",
      "title": "New writes are searchable immediately",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/docs/API.md#post-v1query"
    },
    {
      "category": "Concurrency",
      "id": 15,
      "text": "Each write carries a request ID. Resending a retained request returns its original outcome instead of applying its mutations again. The retry window is bounded.",
      "title": "Retry without applying a write twice",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/docs/API.md#request-ids-and-retries"
    },
    {
      "category": "Concurrency",
      "id": 16,
      "text": "Admission limits count queued and active operations and their encoded payload bytes. Requests that exceed available capacity return overload instead of creating an unbounded queue.",
      "title": "Bound concurrent work",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/DESIGN.md#bounded-concurrent-admission-m16"
    },
    {
      "category": "Concurrency",
      "id": 17,
      "text": "Glider establishes single-writer ownership of each collection. A takeover fences earlier writers, while queries can execute concurrently on published snapshots.",
      "title": "One committer owns each collection",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/docs/API.md#consistency"
    },
    {
      "category": "Getting started",
      "id": 18,
      "text": "Run the Glider server on port 8080 with a mounted Docker volume to preserve local data. Then write points with curl and issue your first vector query.",
      "title": "Start Glider with Docker",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/docs/INSTALL.md"
    },
    {
      "category": "Getting started",
      "id": 19,
      "text": "The dependency-free Python client creates collections, upserts vectors and metadata, and returns nearest neighbors. Each collection selects its dimensions and distance metric.",
      "title": "Use the Python client",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/README.md#quickstart"
    },
    {
      "category": "Getting started",
      "id": 20,
      "text": "Open localhost:8080/console to browse your collections and points, run queries, and inspect the Glider server from your browser.",
      "title": "Browse collections in the console",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/docs/API.md#get-console"
    },
    {
      "category": "Getting started",
      "id": 21,
      "text": "Glider supports S3-compatible object storage. Configure a bucket and a nonoverlapping namespace prefix; the service must provide strongly consistent reads and conditional object creation.",
      "title": "Run on S3 or MinIO",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/docs/INSTALL.md"
    },
    {
      "category": "Getting started",
      "id": 22,
      "text": "The glider-mcp client exposes remember, recall and forget tools to MCP clients. Memories survive restarts and request IDs support safe retries within the retained window.",
      "title": "Give agents durable memory",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/README.md#agent-memory-mcp"
    },
    {
      "category": "Getting started",
      "id": 23,
      "text": "Set profile: true on a query to include its execution mode, elapsed time, queue wait and remote I/O counters. These counters describe the reads caused by that query.",
      "title": "Inspect query I/O",
      "url": "https://github.com/omerfeyzioglu/glider/blob/main/docs/API.md#post-v1query"
    }
  ],
